review note (2026-11-28):
  I reviewed the current Wayland/null backends and the recent lifecycle
  changes. API tests are 9/9 and unit tests are 7/7 when built serially.
  Keep different -Dbackend builds serial: src/backend_selected.zig is shared,
  so parallel builds can overwrite the selector (the compiler now reports it).
  Remaining known gap: tablet.zig removal callbacks only mark objects; the
  Tool/Tablet lists are not pruned until TabletSeat.deinit(). Clipboard
  data-source onSend writes synchronously from the Wayland callback.